1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,283
Start on the Map tab in Omni IC.

2
00:00:02,463 --> 00:00:05,812
It gives the command team a shared view of the department's map.

3
00:00:05,992 --> 00:00:10,493
Open Map Layers when you need to see which kinds of information are being displayed.

4
00:00:10,813 --> 00:00:17,171
The switches let you choose which calls, units, stations, points of interest, and department layers you see.

5
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:22,343
The count at the top gives you a quick check before you interpret an empty part of the map.

6
00:00:22,663 --> 00:00:25,265
Turn off Points of interest to reduce clutter.

7
00:00:25,445 --> 00:00:28,325
The count drops from six to five active layers.

8
00:00:28,505 --> 00:00:31,876
Turn it back on when you need to see saved locations again.

9
00:00:32,196 --> 00:00:34,948
Open the main menu and choose Custom Maps.

10
00:00:35,128 --> 00:00:40,483
This takes you from the department map to the site references your department has made available.

11
00:00:40,803 --> 00:00:44,600
Under Indoor Maps, open the Community Coordination Centre.

12
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:47,319
This example is a fictional floor plan.

13
00:00:47,499 --> 00:00:52,107
In your department, confirm you have the right site before sharing a room reference.

14
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:55,371
The Ground Floor tab shows the plan and room names.

15
00:00:55,551 --> 00:00:59,049
A search team could use this to agree on a briefing location.

16
00:00:59,229 --> 00:01:03,475
A security team could use it to give another shift a precise handoff point.

17
00:01:03,795 --> 00:01:07,485
The tabs at the top switch among the saved floor and data layers.

18
00:01:07,665 --> 00:01:10,460
Here, the GIS Import tab is selected.

19
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:14,181
Check the selected tab before describing what the map shows.

20
00:01:14,501 --> 00:01:17,467
Back on the Custom Maps list, open Search Maps.

21
00:01:17,647 --> 00:01:19,737
Choose Indoor and search for Briefing.

22
00:01:19,917 --> 00:01:24,888
The result includes the site and floor, which helps distinguish rooms with similar names.

23
00:01:25,208 --> 00:01:27,043
Open the briefing room result.

24
00:01:27,223 --> 00:01:31,959
IC returns to the matching floor and shows the saved zone name and description.

25
00:01:32,139 --> 00:01:34,635
This identifies a place on the floor plan.

26
00:01:34,815 --> 00:01:36,841
It does not show who is in that room.

27
00:01:37,161 --> 00:01:40,959
For outdoor coordination, open Weather Alerts from the menu.

28
00:01:41,139 --> 00:01:46,301
Use the search box, severity tabs, or sort choices to find the alert you need.

29
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:49,383
These are fictional alerts for a software exercise.

30
00:01:49,703 --> 00:01:51,175
Select the Severe tab.

31
00:01:51,355 --> 00:01:54,469
The list now shows only the severe exercise alert.

32
00:01:54,649 --> 00:01:57,956
Open it to check what area it covers and when it applies.

33
00:01:58,276 --> 00:02:02,201
Check the effective time, expiry, affected area, and sender.

34
00:02:02,381 --> 00:02:04,621
This example is marked Expired.

35
00:02:04,801 --> 00:02:14,188
Community outreach teams, wildland contractors, and industrial response teams can use the same checks when planning work around changing conditions.
